&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Art Director&lt;/strong&gt; to join our art team. Working with the Senior Art Director and creative leadership, you’ll help shape the game’s visual identity and guide art from early development through delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on creative direction, visual judgment, and alignment across disciplines. You’ll translate the artistic vision into clear briefs, references, reviews, and actionable feedback. You’ll also contribute hands-on in at least one art discipline, moving between high-level direction and detailed critique, paintovers, or blockouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Senior Art Director and creative leadership to define the game’s visual identity, principles, style guides, briefs, references, and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align art disciplines and partner teams around shared goals, dependencies, handoffs, and decisions. Lead visual reviews, critiques, kickoffs, and alignment sessions with clear, constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the creation and refinement of characters, environments, props, lighting, animation, VFX, UI, and other visual components, maintaining cohesion and variety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with design, narrative, engineering, production, and external development partners to carry the artistic intent through development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute hands-on through concept development, paintovers, blockouts, callout sheets, reference packages, prototypes, or other art tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with production and discipline leads to understand milestones, surface risks, and keep creative priorities moving toward delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support artists, external partners, and vendors with clear direction, feedback, and mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve visual review and direction processes, represent the art team in cross-functional discussions, and communicate priorities to artists, partners, and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience creating art for games, animation, film, or a related visual medium, or equivalent experience, with a record of taking on increasing creative responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping define, communicate, and execute an artistic vision from early development through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience in at least one art discipline, with particular relevance to character art, environment art, or both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate visual direction, facilitate constructive reviews, and collaborate with multidisciplinary teams, external partners, and distributed contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of production planning, prioritization, and milestone constraints, with the judgment to balance creative priorities and delivery needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating or contributing to art bibles, style guides, visual development packages, mood boards, paintovers, callout sheets, or similar direction-setting materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of game art and real-time production pipelines, plus familiarity with relevant 2D and/or 3D content creation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that demonstrates artistic judgment, visual problem-solving, hands-on craft, and the ability to guide work from concept to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in mobile game development or art direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Unity game engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting live service content development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
