&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Game Designer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our new unannounced project in Barcelona, Spain, on a hybrid basis, working 3 days a week from the hub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are in development stages on an ambitious, unannounced, cross-platform Strategy/MMO title, creating a team of talented and passionate game makers to join us on this exciting journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Associate Designer that is eager to design, develop, and deliver top quality features and economy models for our new unannounced cross-platform strategy/MMO title. You will write feature design documentation, defining systems that can support a live game model, and balancing economies to scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product, Engineering, Art, Analytics, LiveOps and QA to bring compelling features from concept to release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and update design specs that contain the right level of detail while staying concise and easy to understand for the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive feature optimizations to maintain gameplay quality, improve balance, and boost player engagement (levels &amp;amp; puzzles, battle pass, weekly and daily challenges, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a Design Owner mentality, ensuring designs meet the player’s needs, the franchise strategy and the business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the most recent market trends and best practices to create the best possible designs for our roadmap features, and to bring new ideas to the table&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with senior-level economy and systems designers to craft world-class gameplay and deliver a balanced play experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define solutions within a defined space and identify high ROI improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for scale: plan for long-term content extensibility and system health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep passion for game systems and mechanics across mobile and PC&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of experience designing game systems or balancing game economies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to gather feedback, align stakeholders, and iterate collaboratively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for playing and analyzing games across multiple genres and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently while thriving in a highly collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of free-to-play monetization mechanics including game balancing and virtual economy management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love for strategy games such as 4X or RTS games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile game systems and design sensibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
