&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Compensation Partner, Scopely Explore &lt;/strong&gt;to join our Total Rewards team in Mexico City, Mexico, on a hybrid basis, with three days per week in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make sure our teams have everything they need to create amazing games. The People team manages everything from benefits &amp;amp; employee engagement to professional development opportunities and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the dedicated compensation partner for Scopely Explore, understanding team needs and translating compensation programs into clear guidance and timely support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review job requisitions and new-hire offers, assess compensation inputs, identify exceptions or risks and provide data-informed recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual and mid-year compensation cycles and administer bonuses and performance-based incentives, from planning through reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate equity-vesting data, resolve discrepancies and partner with Payroll to reconcile compensation-related payroll inputs accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compensation models and scenarios to support integration decisions and transitions between compensation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain compensation data accuracy and governance in Workday through controls, audits and process documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll, Finance, Legal, People Business Partners, HR Technology and Recruiting to resolve issues, coordinate dependencies and deliver compensation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and standardize compensation processes, identify automation opportunities and use AI-assisted workflows to improve speed and quality while maintaining human oversight, data safeguards and output validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated compensation knowledge and quantitative analysis skills, supported by 3+ years of experience in compensation, total rewards analytics, finance, investment banking or another closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning complex data into clear recommendations and supporting job-requisition and offer reviews, compensation cycles, incentives, equity-related processes or comparable compensation operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel and experience with human resources information systems or compensation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of maintaining accurate data, applying controls and documenting processes, with attention to detail when identifying and resolving discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain compensation topics clearly to different audiences in writing and conversation, collaborate across functions and manage competing priorities while maintaining accuracy and meeting deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience, operating or improving agentic AI workflows in a business setting. You must be able to design safe workflows, define the agent&#39;s steps, place human approvals at appropriate points, safeguard sensitive data, validate outputs, handle failures, document the workflow and measure accuracy and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Business, Finance or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong English language skills are required for this role, as we have a highly diverse, global business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the gaming, technology or entertainment industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday experience. Workday Advanced Compensation experience is an additional advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Compensation Professional (CCP) or a comparable compensation certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting compensation integration or plan-transition work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, R or other tools used for data analysis and workflow automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
