&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a talented &lt;strong&gt;Design Director, World Systems&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team on an exciting unannounced title built on a globally recognized IP in our Culver City hub, or remotely within the US.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day — whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Design Director, World Systems&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the design of procedural world generation — the systems and craft that combine terrain, creatures, props, resources, buildings, encounters, and points of interest into a cohesive, playable world. You will be hands-on from day one, partner closely with Tools to build the frameworks and tuning levers the team needs, and grow your team over time to serve the needs of the project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the player experience of generated worlds and raise it to a standard that feels authored, readable, and worth exploring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how diverse world elements (terrain, creatures, props, resources, buildings, encounters, POIs) compose into a cohesive whole rather than a pile of systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and enforce world-design standards for density, gameplay pacing, traversal distances, sightlines, landmarking, and encounter/POI placement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Tools team to specify generation frameworks, authoring workflows, and the levers designers use to tune procedural output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work end-to-end in an iterative process — from earliest world concepts and prototypes through directing designers in implementation and live iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong level-design sensibility to procedural space: how far players walk, what they see, when the world breathes, and when it demands attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow a design-thinking methodology to understand player needs, ideate, and propose solutions that meet both player and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand our audience at a deep, empathetic level, and formulate world solutions that serve different player segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closely partner with Creative Director, UX Director, Director of Product, Technical Director, and Content / Adventure leadership so world systems land cleanly in the full player experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Envision and direct world-generation designs that can sustain a large live-operated game, with scalable quality and a scalable content pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand game engine and performance boundaries, and propose creative solutions that work within them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Art, UX, Tools, and Engineering to prototype specific world behaviors early — so the team can feel density, pacing, and composition before full production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the design of multiple world systems at once, ideating on new generation problems while overseeing development of others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a culture of top-quality specification for all relevant design documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, empower, and grow a team of game designers to produce the best possible quality of world and level experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of game design leadership on large-scale worlds (open world, procedural world, action RPG, MMORPG, or comparable adventure / survival spaces)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience leading level design, world design, or encounter placement at a high craft bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience shipping worlds that combine authored intent with generated or assembled content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10 years working on shipped new or live game products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience iterating on ideas in the early phases of development, in a tightly collaborative environment, as well as working on production or live-operated games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts for gameplay pacing, world density, traversal, and sightlines — and the ability to turn those instincts into tunable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with tools or engineering teams to define world-building frameworks, pipelines, or generation levers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define and ensure standards of excellence in design documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with procedural generation systems, world-composition tools, or content-assembly pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on major IP, navigating the competing pressures of player expectations and the need to innovate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years working in Free to Play&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on cross-platform products, and console / PC games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly in Unity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$164,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$247,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
