&lt;li&gt;Define and drive test strategy, coverage, and risk-based validation approaches across features, content, and technical initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a shift-left approach, actively contributing during design and early development phases to identify risks, gaps, and quality concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach validation with a product and player-first mindset, evaluating features not just from a QA perspective but from an end-user and business impact standpoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Design, and Art to influence quality decisions, ensuring alignment with player expectations and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish, maintain, and analyze quality metrics and reports (defect leakage, coverage, cycle time, live issues), ensuring data is tracked effectively and used to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own release quality and risk assessment, providing clear recommendations and participating in Go/No-Go decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation and efficiency initiatives, including leveraging modern tools and exploring AI-driven approaches to improve scalability and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and collaborate with external QA partners, ensuring clear expectations, high-quality output, and effective utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong visibility across stakeholders by proactively communicating progress, risks, and blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of QA experience, including 3+ years in a QA leadership or people-management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build, lead, mentor, and upskill QA teams while driving performance and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in team planning, task prioritization, capacity management, and cross-functional coordination across multiple pods or workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance strategic QA leadership with hands-on testing, debugging, and critical release validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern QA practices, including risk-based testing, shift-left testing, test strategy, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-oriented and player-centric mindset, with the ability to assess quality from user experience, business impact, and release-risk perspectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining, tracking, and using quality metrics, dashboards, and reports to drive decisions and improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning release quality, risk assessments, and providing clear Go/No-Go recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management, communication, problem-solving, and ability to communicate risks, progress, and blockers proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with Jira, test management systems, defect management, and QA reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
