&lt;p&gt;Scopely is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Marketing Data Scientist&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Marketing Analytics&lt;/strong&gt; team in &lt;strong&gt;Barcelona, Spain&lt;/strong&gt;, on a hybrid basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing, and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people worldwide daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Marketing Data Scientist, you will be part of the Marketing Analytics team, which is responsible for executing the cross-portfolio analytics initiatives for Scopely’s User Acquisition and Ads teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;develop and maintain models that guide paid media investment, including spend-response curves, player lifetime value forecasts, user acquisition forecasts, and budget optimization approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;measure the effectiveness and incremental impact of advertising using sound statistical methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;work on Ads initiatives to improve player experience while optimizing monetization, enhance our strategy in ads bidding, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;translate model outputs into clear recommendations on where and when to invest, explaining expected outcomes, uncertainty, and key assumptions to marketing and finance partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;partner with User Acquisition, Ads, Finance, and Analytics Engineering teams to turn reliable data science into tools and workflows that support recurring marketing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a Data Scientist. Background in performance marketing and mobile free-to-play gaming is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with a track record of using data to drive meaningful outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;preferred experience in applying marketing modeling techniques e.g., media mix modeling, time series forecasting, segmentation/clustering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;advanced SQL and hands-on Python skills for working with large datasets, developing analyses, and building reliable, scalable models; exposure to Google Cloud Platform and BigQuery is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;working knowledge of visualization tools: Looker (Preferred), QlikView, Tableau, or PowerBI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;proficiency in developing and operating production data science workflows, including orchestration with tools such as Airflow and containerization with Docker; cloud deployment, CI/CD, and monitoring experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;strong communication skills and the ability to explain clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, influencing decision-making through structured storytelling and data-evidence-based recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a quantitative or scientific field, or equivalent practical experience, is a big plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience in the games industry, or interest in video/mobile games and the evolving in-game advertising field, is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! &amp;nbsp; We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
