&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Director of Performance Marketing&lt;/strong&gt; for a new, unannounced casual mobile game to join our Performance Marketing Team in Barcelona on a &lt;strong&gt;Hybrid basis&lt;/strong&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people worldwide daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Performance Marketing team is focused on driving player growth and efficiency across various digital marketing channels. The teams are based in Europe and the US.&amp;nbsp; The UA team’s mobile advertising ecosystem is an always-changing, rapidly growing world, and at Scopely, you&#39;ll play a key part in our next big leap in user growth. Our mission is to make experiences that our players love and keep coming back to time and time again.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the Performance Marketing team based in Barcelona for a new casual mobile game launching. This role works cross-functionally with Product, Finance, Analytics, Growth Marketing and Data Engineering and is part of the Performance Marketing team at Scopely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the global game team and lead the performance marketing team for a new, unannounced title based on an IP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will lead performance marketing efforts for this title, driving global user growth and building scalable acquisition strategies from pre-launch through live operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop UA strategy, methodology and processes to deliver on each game’s performance targets and improve team’s capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring leading analysis and insight to acquisition funnel measurement, including helping to define &amp;amp; set goals for key performance indicators on each game, and working with Analytics on implementing improved Business Intelligence and Data Science predictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor the performance marketing managers to identify gaps and inefficiencies in campaign creation, analysis and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as key team leader offering feedback, guidance &amp;amp; coaching, and industry mentorship to Scopely’s Barcelona-based UA team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive relentless culture of experimentation on all key existing UA channels (ex.: Facebook, Google, mobile ad networks, ad exchanges, offerwall) while also ideating and establishing new user acquisition funnels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Strategic Marketing, Finance, Analytics, Marketing Creative, and Data Engineering teams to align the UA strategy with game positioning, audience targeting, lifecycle marketing, and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deep analytical insights into campaign performance, working with Analytics and Data Science to improve forecasting and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally to enhance creative strategy, marketing technology, automation, and fraud prevention systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and optimize multi-million-dollar marketing budgets with a focus on ROI and long-term player value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of performance marketing / user acquisition experience, ideally within mobile gaming or consumer apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of people management experience, with a track record of building and leading high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep analytical mindset with experience in attribution, incrementality testing, LTV modeling, and performance forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with major platforms (Meta, Google, TikTok, programmatic networks, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in launching, and scaling new products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, communication, and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to effectively manage and optimize a multi-million dollar acquisition budgets across multiple channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive major incremental volume &amp;amp; returns from improvements in automation, marketing tech stack, fraud prevention, or analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preference (but not required) for experience with match-3, puzzle or other casual mobile games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! &amp;nbsp; We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
