&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Central Studio Operations provides shared operational support, processes, and resources that help Scopely’s game studios work efficiently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;It coordinates cross-functional teams and enables the successful development, launch, and ongoing operation of games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as an internal driver and strategic partner to our game studios. Drawing on deep, hands-on experience in the LiveOps lifecycle, you will lead the design and deployment of our global LiveOps Quality OS. You will ensure every event, campaign, and content update, from initial production and testing to live deployment and post-launch monitoring, gets the attention it needs from a Quality Assurance perspective and meets the highest bar for player experience, stability, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is an operational mastermind who thrives on influence without authority. You are equally comfortable talking dev pipelines with engineers, discussing risk mitigation with LiveOps and Product leaders, and driving strategic alignment with external vendors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Strategic Alignment: Partner directly with Game Team Leadership and Executive Producers to align release practices and quality standards with Scopely’s global business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-End LiveOps Quality &amp;amp; Performance: Review the operational rigor of live service releases. Ensure robust processes are in place across the full LiveOps lifecycle (from campaign/event configuration and QA/testing to live deployment, telemetry validation, and real-time performance monitoring)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect the Release OS: Define, iterate, and champion the adoption of standardized, modern release frameworks and deployment processes across all titles. Focus heavily on risk mitigation, live-environment stability, and real-time incident monitoring to prevent player-impacting downtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence Without Authority: Act as a central change agent, guiding cross-functional studio teams across global locations to adopt modern quality operations principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize External Partnerships: Manage strategic relationships with trusted external QA and development partners. Design service level agreements and workflows to ensure external teams operate as seamless, high-performing extensions of our studios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Modernization &amp;amp; AI Initiatives: Champion the strategic integration of automation, AI-driven testing, and modern tooling into the studio release pipelines to aggressively drive down time-to-market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Root Cause Analysis: Conduct continuous post-mortems and root-cause analyses on release bottlenecks, turning data insights into actionable, studio-wide process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for Operational Excellence: Act as the primary spokesperson for central operations, clearly communicating release risks, deployment health metrics, and strategic improvements to executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LiveOps &amp;amp; Games Experience: Proven track record of managing live-service games on mobile. Strong hands-on experience leading campaigns and events through the entire lifecycle, from initial concept and implementation to testing, release, and live performance monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Power of Influence: A proven track record of driving massive process changes and operational improvements across matrixed organizations without direct line-management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production &amp;amp; Operations Acumen: Strong background in Technical Program Management, Release Engineering, or Technical Production. You understand CI/CD pipelines, build distribution, and deployment risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Partner Management: Extensive experience collaborating with, evaluating, and maximizing the value of large-scale external partners and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems Thinking: The ability to look at a highly complex, multi-studio ecosystem, identify systemic inefficiencies, and engineer elegant, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master Communicator: Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to translate technical risks into clear, business-focused narratives for executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LiveOps Backends &amp;amp; Remote Config: Hands-on experience with systems like Azure PlayFab, Unity Gaming Services, Firebase, or proprietary internal LiveOps dashboards desirable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; BI Tools: Proficiency with product analytics platforms (Amplitude, Mixpanel, or GameAnalytics) and BI visualization tools (Tableau, Looker, or Excel/Google Sheets) desirable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production &amp;amp; Operations: Experience managing workflows in JIRA and using build distribution tools (TestFlight, Google Play Console, Firebase App Distribution) desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree level education or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for mobile and console/PC games, with proven experience working on games as a live service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LiveOps QA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to generate impact and make progress through influence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a portfolio of projects or in a central capacity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to oversee and manage projects with complex setups&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong accountability in observing deadlines and engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience in a game development environment with proven experience in management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very strong interpersonal and communication skills (both written and verbally) and ability to collaborate with senior management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify risks and changes needed and to execute solutions, with appropriate sense of urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and demonstrated knowledge of project management, software development methodologies, QA best known practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with setting up and navigating through JIRA, TestRail, Google Docs, Google Sheets/Excel, and a build distribution management system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior IT Procurement Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Sourcing &amp;amp; Procurement team, embedded within the IT department, in Barcelona on a hybrid basis!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The IT/Ops team keeps everything behind the scenes running smoothly and we make sure all teams are equipped and connected - whether across the office or halfway around the world. AV struggles? Don’t worry, we’ve got this.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a Senior IT Procurement Specialist, you will help Scopely make informed, cost-effective technology purchasing decisions across our global business. Working closely with IT, Legal, Finance, and Security, you will manage the end-to-end procurement lifecycle for enterprise software, SaaS, hardware, and IT services. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your work will help strengthen vendor partnerships, optimise technology spend, manage commercial risk, and ensure our teams have access to the technology and services they need.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead technology sourcing:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with IT and business stakeholders to understand requirements, develop sourcing strategies, and manage RFI, RFP, and RFQ processes across enterprise technology categories.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate and manage vendors:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess suppliers based on technical capabilities, security, pricing, service quality, and delivery performance while building strong vendor relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Negotiate commercial agreements:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead negotiations covering pricing, contractual terms, service-level agreements, and renewals. Partner with Legal to review and redline vendor contracts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize technology spend:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct total cost of ownership analyses, evaluate licensing models, and identify savings opportunities through vendor consolidation, rate optimization, and license rationalization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage contracts and renewals:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain accurate contract records, licensing entitlements, and renewal schedules while proactively managing contract renewals and true-ups.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support global procurement operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary procurement partner for IT stakeholders across the US, EMEA, and APAC, collaborating with Legal, Finance, and Security to support procurement decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain procurement compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Support purchase requisitions, invoice resolution, and Enterprise Technology purchasing cards, including spend monitoring, reconciliation, and adherence to procurement policies and approval requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve procurement processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to improvements in sourcing workflows, procurement reporting, contract management, and purchasing processes to increase efficiency and transparency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Supply Chain Management, Business Administration, Information Technology, or a related field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;5–7 years of experience in IT procurement, strategic sourcing, or technology contract management, including enterprise software, SaaS, hardware, or IT services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of enterprise technology categories and the ability to translate technical requirements into effective sourcing strategies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated success negotiating technology agreements and delivering measurable cost savings and favorable commercial terms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Experience reviewing technology contracts, including MSAs, SaaS and licensing agreements, SLAs, DPAs, and proof-of-concept agreements, in partnership with Legal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strong analytical capabilities, including total cost of ownership modeling, spend analysis, and business case development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with procure-to-pay processes, procurement and contract management platforms, and SaaS management tools.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, stakeholder management, and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple sourcing initiatives independently across global teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
